# Painted metal: principled bases of measured metals under tinted clear coats
# (Beer-Lambert through the coat: deeper color at grazing angles). Copper
# paint over aluminium (the studio car's rims), a candy red over chrome, a
# half-metallic titanium under a blue coat, a rough coat over gold, and a
# tinted coat over a Schlick white base. Lit like clearcoat.scene. Mitsuba has
# no tinted coat and no measured metal in its principled, so only the
# same-model comparison is made.

image_width  384
aspect_ratio 2
samples_per_pixel 512
max_depth    64
background   0.1 0.1 0.12

camera lookfrom 0 2.2 9  lookat 0 0.6 0  vup 0 1 0  vfov 24

material floor  lambertian 0.5 0.5 0.5
material wall   lambertian 0.35 0.3 0.25
material lamp   emissive 5 5 5
material bulb   emissive 40 30 20
material rim    principled metallic 1 conductor Al roughness 0.35 clearcoat 1 clearcoat_roughness 0.2 clearcoat_color 0.6 0.35 0.28
material candy  principled metallic 1 conductor Cr roughness 0.2 clearcoat 1 clearcoat_color 0.7 0.1 0.1
material blue   principled color 0.5 0.5 0.5 metallic 0.5 conductor Ti roughness 0.5 clearcoat 0.7 clearcoat_color 0.4 0.5 0.9
material gold   principled metallic 1 conductor Au roughness 0.3 clearcoat 1 clearcoat_roughness 0.4 clearcoat_color 0.9 0.8 0.6
material white  principled color 0.9 0.9 0.9 roughness 0.4 clearcoat 1 clearcoat_color 0.5 0.8 0.5

quad -10 0 -10   20 0 0   0 0 20   floor
quad -10 0 -3    20 0 0   0 6 0    wall
quad -2 5 -1     4 0 0    0 0 3    lamp
sphere 2.6 2.2 1.2  0.15  bulb

sphere -2.4 0.55 0    0.55  rim
sphere -1.2 0.55 0    0.55  candy
sphere  0.0 0.55 0    0.55  blue
sphere  1.2 0.55 0    0.55  gold
sphere  2.4 0.55 0    0.55  white
